{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grecolatinovivo-create/emendando-catalogo/manifesti/data/manifesti/romani-pas/607827.json","type":"Manifest","label":{"none":["PAS DENO-C47328: Roman Finger Ring"]},"metadata":[{"label":{"it":["Oggetto"]},"value":{"none":["anello"]}},{"label":{"it":["Supporto"]},"value":{"none":["metallo (anello)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Datazione"]},"value":{"none":["100-300 d.C."]}},{"label":{"it":["Provenienza"]},"value":{"none":["contea di ritrovamento: Lincolnshire (Inghilterra e Galles)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Descrizione"]},"value":{"none":["TREASURE CASE 2014 T197: An incomplete Roman silver finger ring dating to the second or third century AD. Only the bezel and part of one shoulder survives. The surviving shoulder of the finger ring is lightly arched and tapers inwards towards the missing hoop - The finger ring was probably D-shaped rather than circular in outline, typical for Roman Finger rings of this period. Due to peripheral wear and damage the shape of the bezel is uncertain but appears to be rounded at the edges and has a square incised outline framing the centre. This square outline contains an incised O at the centre and has faint traces of additional incised lines around this. It is suggested that this ring is an…"]}},{"label":{"it":["Identificativo PAS"]},"value":{"none":["DENO-C47328"]}},{"label":{"it":["FindID"]},"value":{"none":["607827"]}}],"requiredStatement":{"label":{"it":["Attribuzione"]},"value":{"it":["Portable Antiquities Scheme / The Trustees of the British Museum (Portable Antiquities Scheme, finds.org.uk). Foto: The Portable Antiquities Scheme, Charlotte Burrill, 2014-03-21 14:07:08, CC BY-SA 4.0 ; The Portable Antiquities Scheme, Charlotte Burrill, 2014-03-21 14:07:08, CC BY-SA 2.0, da Wikimedia Commons. Manifesto scritto da Emendando."]}},"homepage":[{"id":"https://finds.org.uk/database/artefacts/record/id/607827","type":"Text","label":{"none":["PAS DENO-